<title>CHINA: China '97 crude demand seen at 158 mln tonnes.</title>
<headline>China '97 crude demand seen at 158 mln tonnes.</headline>
<dateline>BEIJING 1997-02-04</dateline>
<text>
<p>China's crude oil demand is expected to be 158.2 million tonnes in 1997 while production is forecast to be 152.5 million tonnes, the Farmers Daily newspaper said on Tuesday.</p>
<p>The State Statistical Bureau has said 1996 output was 158.51 million tonnes, up 6.37 percent compared with 1995.</p>
<p>Domestic production of coal was expected to reach 1.37 billion tonnes in 1997 while demand would hit 1.266 billion tonnes, up by 39 million tonnes from the previous year, the Farmers Daily said.</p>
<p>China produced 1.374 billion tonnes of coal in 1996, up 6.37 percent from 1995.</p>
<p>($1=8.3 yuan)</p>
<p>-- Beijing newsroom (8610) 6532-1921</p>
